From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0334/0334] SableOS: no padlock on the lock screen without a
 fingerprint sensor

The Android lock icon sat on top of the locked glance ("Unlock to read message
details") on the Q25's short screen. Without an under-display fingerprint
sensor it has no job (Enter unlocks), so it is kept in the layout at one pixel.
---
 .../ui/view/layout/sections/DefaultDeviceEntrySection.kt | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/ui/view/layout/sections/DefaultDeviceEntrySection.kt b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/ui/view/layout/sections/DefaultDeviceEntrySection.kt
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/ui/view/layout/sections/DefaultDeviceEntrySection.kt
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/ui/view/layout/sections/DefaultDeviceEntrySection.kt
@@ -165,6 +165,10 @@ constructor(
                 iconRadiusPx * scaleFactor,
                 constraintSet,
             )
+            // SableOS: without an under-display fingerprint sensor the padlock has no job, and on a
+            // short screen it sat on top of the locked glance. It stays in the layout at one pixel.
+            constraintSet.constrainWidth(deviceEntryIconViewId, 1)
+            constraintSet.constrainHeight(deviceEntryIconViewId, 1)
         }
     }
 
